.git
.gitignore
build/
dist/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Build output and caches that .gitignore already keeps out of the repository. They are not
# in the image either way - nothing copies them - but everything here is uploaded to the
# daemon as the build context before the first instruction runs, and these are the large
# ones: editors/vscode/out/ from working on the extension, htmlcov/ and .coverage from a
# coverage run, the packaged extension, the built documentation, and the two ASAP2
# specification pdfs under the design records.
editors/vscode/out/
*.vsix
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml
coverage.json
docs/_build/
docs/superpowers/*.pdf
# What npm leaves in the tree, which the image makes for itself: its pages stage installs the
# packages of gui/, generates the page types, checks the pages against them and compiles them,
# and the final stage takes the pages from it. `COPY src` and `COPY gui` take whatever the
# context holds. The host's packages would land on the ones `npm ci` installed before them -
# packages npm installed for another system. The host's pages and types would land first, and
# the image's own would be written over them file by file, leaving whatever the host had that
# the image does not write: a stale build's pages installed beside the fresh ones, the types of
# a file format the package no longer has, checked with the rest. **/ because a bare
# node_modules/ matches at the root only, where there is none: the extension's and the browser
# interface's are further down.
**/node_modules/
src/ddd/gui/static/
gui/src/generated/
# What running the browser tests and building the widget workbench leave, Playwright's traces
# and report and Ladle's static build: nothing the image uses, and copied into its pages stage
# by `COPY gui` otherwise.
gui/test-results/
gui/playwright-report/
gui/ladle-build/
